      "content": "Let's use the Civil Rights Movement as a revolutionary example, where activists like MLK strategically challenged unjust laws to achieve guaranteed equality for everyone. In contrast, you could frame the Jim Crow systems and Resistance Groups as regressive because they actively worked to reinforce social inequality and resist civil rights advancements. By comparing their specific goals—equality versus preservation of status quo—students can clearly see how progressive efforts aim to fix systemic issues while regressive ones block necessary change. This side-by-side analysis will make the abstract concepts of social movements much more tangible for your students.",
