      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A powerful example is the American Luddites, whose \"regressive\" label now obscures their rational defense of their livelihoods against machines they feared would destroy their jobs. While modern class critiques call them anti-progress, they operated on a logical view that economic survival and community well-being should not be compromised by technological disruption. Using this with a contemporary example like school budget protests shows students that resistance often has valid, self-protective reasons even when it opposes rapid social shifts. This distinction helps them understand that arguing for stability or gradual change doesn't make a movement inherently negative, but rather highlights differing values about progress.",
